{"name":"Hephaestus","hex":"#e1d4b6","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Hephaestus","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The god of fire, smithwork, metallurgy, volcanoes, and artisans, who served as blacksmith of the gods. His Roman counterpart is Vulcan."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Hephaestus"}],"entries":[{"title":"Hephaestus","blocks":[{"text":"Hephaestus is the Greek god of artisans, blacksmiths, carpenters, craftsmen, fire, metallurgy, metalworking, sculpture, and volcanoes. In Greek mythology, Hephaestus was the son of Hera, either on her own or by her husband Zeus. He was cast off Mount Olympus by his mother Hera because of his lameness, the result of a congenital impairment, or in another account, by Zeus for protecting Hera from his advances."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/Hephaistos_Thetis_at_Kylix_by_the_Foundry_Painter_Antikensammlung_Berlin_F2294.jpg/330px-Hephaistos_Thetis_at_Kylix_by_the_Foundry_Painter_Antikensammlung_Berlin_F2294.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hephaestus","wikidata":"Q44384"},{"title":"Hephaestus (fish)","blocks":[{"text":"Hephaestus is a genus of freshwater ray-finned fish, grunters from the family Terapontidae."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/FMIB_36165_Therapon_carbo.jpeg/330px-FMIB_36165_Therapon_carbo.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hephaestus_(fish)","wikidata":"Q10522199"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Atenas%2C_%C3%81gora_03.jpg/500px-Atenas%2C_%C3%81gora_03.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Atenas%2C_%C3%81gora_03.jpg/1280px-Atenas%2C_%C3%81gora_03.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_camp